ce:section.ce:para:
The hydrolytic enzymes from P. chlororaphis responsible for Impranil degradationwere analyzed for polyurethanase activity by Impranil zymograms using ND–PAGE gels. TheImpranil zymogram revealed three migrating bands, with R
                        f values of 0.25, 0.417and 0.917 (Fig. 2
                        ). All three bands conferred beta zones of clearing. No band of alpha clearing was noted.

Ammonium sulfate was added to the cell-free culture supernatant to give 60% saturation. Theprecipitated proteins were dialyzed and the crude enzyme preparation fractionated by anion exchange.Two peaks of protein activity were detected. The first peak of activity conferred a beta zone ofclearing on a polyurethane agarose plate (Fig. 3
                        ) and also displayed protease activity against hide powder azure. No esterase activity was observed.The second peak of activity conferred an alpha zone of clearing on a polyurethane agar plate Fig. 3 and also displayed esterase activity against r-nitrophenol acetate. No protease activity wasobserved. This second peak of activity was further purified by gel filtration using a SepharoseG75-120 column. The molecular mass of the purified protein as determined by SDS–PAGE wasestimated to be 27 kDa (Fig. 4
                        ).
